  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring the Protection of Women and Girls, Including Survivors of GBV and Trafficking and Vulnerable Communities during the Socio-Economic Crisis in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The joint programme has been designed to provide strengthened access to protection and lifesaving support to vulnerable communities and women and girls at risk and survivors of GBV and trafficking during this complex crisis in Sri Lanka. The interventions seek to provide a lifesaving, survivor-centred, multisectoral approach to integrating risk mitigation actions to ensure women and girls are not exposed to further harm. The response strategy integrates key components of ensuring shelters are strengthened for ongoing operations and able to take in new victims/survivors; psychosocial support services for women and girls at risk and survivors of GBV and trafficking; referral pathways established and popularized for holistic response to survivors of GBV/trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
